domestic neglect;
17. Domestic Neglect is someone who neglects a person within their household, whereas according to the law applicable to them or due to an agreement or contract they are obliged to provide life, care, or maintenance to that person.
In addition, neglect also applies to anyone who causes economic dependence by restricting and/or prohibiting proper work inside or outside the home so that the victim is under the control of that person.

